{%- liquid
  # 'homepage.faq.eyebrow' is the only translation key this section owns and
  # locales/en.default.json is owned elsewhere, so every other label below is
  # either merchant copy declared in the schema or derived from the blocks.
  # Nothing here invents a string a translator has never seen.
  assign head_eyebrow = 'homepage.faq.eyebrow' | t
  assign head_title = section.settings.heading | default: 'Questions, answered'
  assign anchor = section.settings.anchor | default: 'faq'
  assign heading_id = 'FaqTitle-' | append: section.id
-%}

<section id="{{ anchor }}" class="sl-faq" aria-labelledby="{{ heading_id }}">
  <div class="sl-wrap sl-faq__inner">
    {%- comment -%}
      Deliberately not the shared section-head snippet. Nine bands above this
      one open with the same centred eyebrow → h2 → lede and then a grid of
      cards; a tenth repetition is the thing that made the page read as one
      template applied ten times. The heading here is a fixed left rail and
      the questions run in a ruled column beside it, so the FAQ looks like
      the index at the back of a manual rather than another marketing band.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <header class="sl-faq__rail sl-reveal">
      <p class="sl-faq__eyebrow">
        {%- comment -%}
          Not .sl-eyebrow. That shared class paints amber, and amber marks a
          value the engine measured — "BEFORE YOU FILM" is a label, not a
          measurement. Spending the signal on section furniture is exactly
          what trains the eye to read it as decoration.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <span>{{ head_eyebrow }}</span>
        <span class="sl-faq__rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        {%- comment -%}
          Derived, never typed. A hand-written entry count goes stale the
          first time somebody adds a question in the theme editor, and a
          stale number on a page about honesty is a bad trade.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <span class="sl-faq__count" aria-hidden="true">{{ section.blocks.size }}</span>
      </p>
      <h2 id="{{ heading_id }}" class="sl-faq__title">{{ head_title }}</h2>
      {%- if section.settings.lede != blank -%}
        <p class="sl-faq__lede">{{ section.settings.lede }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Both halves are guarded because Shopify's `url` setting type takes no
        default: the label ships with one and the link does not, so an
        un-configured store must render nothing rather than a live control
        pointing at an empty href.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if section.settings.link_label != blank and section.settings.link_url != blank -%}
        <a class="sl-faq__link" href="{{ section.settings.link_url }}">
          <span>{{ section.settings.link_label }}</span>
          <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </header>

    {%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
      <div class="sl-faq__list sl-reveal sl-reveal--d1">
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          <details class="sl-faq__item"{{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
            <summary class="sl-faq__q">
              <span class="sl-faq__num" aria-hidden="true">{%- if forloop.index < 10 -%}0{%- endif -%}{{ forloop.index }}</span>
              <h3 class="sl-faq__q-text">{{ block.settings.question }}</h3>
              <span class="sl-faq__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="sl-faq__a">
              <p>{{ block.settings.answer }}</p>
            </div>
          </details>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%}
  Native <details>/<summary> stays. It carries the disclosure role and the
  expanded state to assistive tech without a line of JavaScript, so the
  accordion still works in the theme editor's re-render, with JS disabled,
  and inside a print or reader view.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      {%- for block in section.blocks %}
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": {{ block.settings.question | json }},
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": {{ block.settings.answer | json }}
        }
      }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
      {%- endfor %}
    ]
  }
</script>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
.sl-faq {
  padding-top: var(--sl-section-space);
  padding-bottom: var(--sl-section-space);
  border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
}
/* The header goes sticky once the page scrolls, so an in-page jump to #faq
   used to land the heading underneath it. */
.sl-faq { scroll-margin-top: var(--sl-space-8); }

.sl-faq__inner {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: clamp(32px, 5vw, 48px);
}
/* 4/8 rather than 6/6: the rail is a label and the questions are the
   content, so the column widths should say which is which. */
@media (min-width: 1000px) {
  .sl-faq__inner {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 4fr) minmax(0, 8fr);
    gap: clamp(40px, 5vw, 80px);
    align-items: start;
  }
  /* Clears the sticky header bar (64px + its padding) so the rail parks
     below it instead of behind it. */
  .sl-faq__rail {
    position: sticky;
    top: var(--sl-space-9);
  }
}

.sl-faq__eyebrow {
  margin: 0 0 var(--sl-space-5);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--sl-space-3);
  color: var(--sl-ink-muted);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-eyebrow-size);
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: var(--sl-eyebrow-track);
  line-height: 1;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}
.sl-faq__rule {
  flex: 1;
  height: 1px;
  background: var(--sl-border-strong);
}
.sl-faq__count {
  color: var(--sl-ink-soft);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

.sl-faq__title {
  margin: 0;
  max-width: 12ch;
  color: var(--sl-ink);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-display);
  font-size: var(--sl-heading-support);
  font-weight: 800;
  letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  line-height: 1.02;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  text-wrap: balance;
}
.sl-faq__lede {
  margin: var(--sl-space-5) 0 0;
  max-width: 36ch;
  color: var(--sl-ink-soft);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-base);
  line-height: 1.6;
  text-wrap: pretty;
}
.sl-faq__link {
  margin-top: var(--sl-space-6);
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--sl-space-2);
  padding-bottom: 6px;
  /* An interactive edge, so --sl-control-border (3.45:1), never the
     decorative 1.33:1 hairline. */
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-control-border);
  color: var(--sl-ink);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  text-decoration: none;
}
.sl-faq__link:hover { border-bottom-color: var(--sl-ink); }

/* ---- the entries ---- */
.sl-faq__list { border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-border-strong); }
/* The rule that divides rail from entries. The rows carry their own inset,
   so the questions never sit on top of it. */
@media (min-width: 1000px) {
  .sl-faq__list { border-left: 1px solid var(--sl-border); }
}
.sl-faq__item {
  position: relative;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
}
.sl-faq__item:last-child { border-bottom-color: var(--sl-border-strong); }

/* An open row SINKS. A cast shadow is invisible against --sl-bg — the old
   card treatment was painting near-black onto near-black — so depth here is
   the darker --sl-night well plus the lit top edge every --sl-shadow-* token
   now leads with. */
.sl-faq__item[open] {
  background: var(--sl-night);
  box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgba(var(--sl-cream-rgb), 0.05);
}
.sl-faq__item[open]::before {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  bottom: -1px;
  left: 0;
  width: 2px;
  background: var(--sl-ink);
}

.sl-faq__q {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 48px minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
  align-items: baseline;
  align-content: center;
  min-height: 68px;
  padding: var(--sl-dense-inset) var(--sl-card-inset);
  color: var(--sl-ink);
  cursor: pointer;
  list-style: none;
  text-align: left;
}
.sl-faq__q::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
.sl-faq__q:hover { background: rgba(var(--sl-cream-rgb), 0.03); }

/* The 48px number track is not a coincidence: .sl-faq__a indents by exactly
   --sl-card-inset + 48px, so the answer's first character lands under the
   question's. Change one and change the other. */
.sl-faq__num {
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  /* NOT amber, which is what this was. Amber marks a value the engine
     measured; the position of a question in a list measures nothing. */
  color: var(--sl-ink-muted);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}
.sl-faq__q:hover .sl-faq__num,
.sl-faq__item[open] .sl-faq__num { color: var(--sl-ink-soft); }

/* A real heading — eleven questions were invisible to heading navigation —
   restyled to sit in the row like the span it replaced. Questions are
   interface type, so they take the sans face rather than the expanded
   display 800 that base.css gives every h3. */
.sl-faq__q-text {
  min-width: 0;
  margin: 0;
  font-family: var(--sl-font-sans);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-lg);
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: -0.012em;
  line-height: 1.35;
  color: inherit;
  text-wrap: pretty;
}

/* Reads as a control, so it takes a control-grade edge even though the
   whole summary is the hit area. align-self opts it out of the row's
   baseline alignment and centres it instead. */
.sl-faq__icon {
  position: relative;
  align-self: center;
  margin-left: var(--sl-space-4);
  width: 22px;
  height: 22px;
  border: 1px solid var(--sl-control-border);
  border-radius: var(--sl-radius-sm);
}
.sl-faq__icon::before,
.sl-faq__icon::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  background: var(--sl-ink-soft);
}
/* 2px strokes in a 20px padding box land on the exact centre. A 1px stroke
   would need a half-pixel offset to centre, and half-pixel nudges are how
   the old sheet drifted off its own scale. */
.sl-faq__icon::before { top: 9px; left: 5px; width: 10px; height: 2px; }
.sl-faq__icon::after { top: 5px; left: 9px; width: 2px; height: 10px; }
.sl-faq__q:hover .sl-faq__icon { border-color: var(--sl-ink-soft); }
.sl-faq__item[open] .sl-faq__icon { border-color: var(--sl-ink); }
.sl-faq__item[open] .sl-faq__icon::before,
.sl-faq__item[open] .sl-faq__icon::after { background: var(--sl-ink); }
/* The plus becoming a minus is state, not decoration, so the transform
   applies unconditionally; only the tween is motion. The old rule declared
   its transition outside any guard. */
.sl-faq__item[open] .sl-faq__icon::after { transform: scaleY(0); }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
  .sl-faq__icon { transition: border-color .2s ease; }
  .sl-faq__icon::before,
  .sl-faq__icon::after { transition: transform .2s ease, background-color .2s ease; }
  .sl-faq__link span:last-child { transition: transform .2s ease; }
  .sl-faq__link:hover span:last-child { transform: translateX(3px); }
}

.sl-faq__a {
  max-width: 74ch;
  padding: 0 var(--sl-card-inset) var(--sl-card-inset) calc(var(--sl-card-inset) + 48px);
  color: var(--sl-ink-soft);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-base);
  line-height: 1.65;
  text-align: left;
  text-wrap: pretty;
}
.sl-faq__a p { margin: 0 0 var(--sl-space-3); }
.sl-faq__a p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.sl-faq__a a { color: var(--sl-ink); }

@media (max-width: 749px) {
  /* The .sl-wrap gutter already insets this column. Paying --sl-card-inset
     on top of it started the questions a quarter of the way across a phone,
     so rows run to the gutter and the number takes a narrower margin —
     answer indent moved in step to keep the two columns aligned. */
  .sl-faq__q {
    grid-template-columns: var(--sl-space-6) minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
    padding-left: 0;
    padding-right: 0;
  }
  .sl-faq__a {
    padding-left: var(--sl-space-6);
    padding-right: 0;
  }
  .sl-faq__icon { margin-left: var(--sl-space-3); }
  .sl-faq__title { max-width: 100%; }
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "FAQ",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "anchor", "label": "Section anchor id", "default": "faq" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Questions, answered" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "lede", "label": "Rail lede", "default": "What people ask before their first upload — filming, reports, plans, gear, and billing." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "link_label", "label": "Rail link label", "default": "Ask us anything" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "link_url", "label": "Rail link (hidden until set)" }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "qa",
      "name": "Question",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "question", "label": "Question", "default": "How should I film my swing?" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "answer", "label": "Answer", "default": "Phone at hip height, face-on, ball on a tee — portrait clips straight off a phone work fine. Down-the-line clips get tempo & rhythm only for now; film face-on for the full report." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 12,
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "FAQ",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How should I film my swing?",
            "answer": "Phone at hip height, face-on, ball on a tee — portrait clips straight off a phone work fine. Down-the-line clips get tempo & rhythm only for now; film face-on for the full report."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do I need to trim the clip first?",
            "answer": "No. Upload the whole clip — CaddieInsight listens for audible strikes and separates detected swings automatically. If a strike is not audible or detection misses it, you can supply a manual strike time."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why do I have to choose a club?",
            "answer": "For irons, hybrids, fairway woods, and drivers, supported club context helps rank responsible coaching. CaddieInsight requires the club before upload and keeps it with the report. A wedge is stored and used for matched comparisons, but its coaching remains neutral until shot intent and lie are captured."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I delete my swing history and start over?",
            "answer": "Yes. Your account includes a deliberate delete-history flow so you can remove prior sessions and restart your practice record."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What does the free plan include?",
            "answer": "One full swing analysis per calendar month, free forever. It produces the complete report: metrics table, key-position strip, centerline overlay, slow motion, and coaching notes. Pro adds unlimited filming; Coach adds the annotated replay, the progress dashboard, and the matched re-film verdict."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What do the paid plans cost?",
            "answer": "Pro is $9.99/month or $69.99 for a full year. Coach is $19.99/month or $139.99/year and adds the replay, the dashboard, and the proof cycle. The Founders Pass is one payment of $249, includes every Coach feature for good, and never renews — only the first 100 members can buy one, because a lifetime product is only honest if the business can afford to keep running it."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does Pro unlock after I buy it here?",
            "answer": "Pro connects to the CaddieInsight account linked to your purchase email. After checkout, open the app to sign in or finish account setup; access activates when the paid order is confirmed."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does it work for left-handed golfers?",
            "answer": "Yes. Choose your handedness when you upload, and every measurement, overlay, and coaching note is computed for a left-handed swing."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does gear take to arrive?",
            "answer": "Training aids ship from partner warehouses. Orders are processed in 1–2 business days and U.S. delivery typically takes 6–12 business days, with tracking emailed at dispatch."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What if a training aid isn't right for me?",
            "answer": "Unused gear may be returned within 30 days. See the Shipping & Returns page for eligibility and instructions."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I get a refund on Pro?",
            "answer": "CaddieInsight Pro and other digital services are refundable within 14 days of purchase if unused."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
